<title>GERMANY: Commerzbank details earnings of major units.</title>
<headline>Commerzbank details earnings of major units.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996. Commerzbank AG on Tuesday gave the following operating profit figures for the parent bank and its major subsidiaries.</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>OPERATING PROFIT</p>
<p> Commerzbank AG (parent bank)	    1,180  vs 875</p>
<p> comdirect bank GmbH*			46 loss vs 42 loss</p>
<p> Commerz Financial Products GmbH	 131    vs 26</p>
<p> Hypothekenbank in Essen AG  109    vs 82</p>
<p> RHEINHYP Rheinische Hypothekenbank AG 307    vs 279</p>
<p> Caisse Centrale de Reescompte S.A.    29     vs 28</p>
<p> Commerzbank International S.A.	  387    vs 392</p>
<p> Commerzbank (Budapest) Rt.		12     vs 9</p>
<p> Commerzbank Europe (Ireland)	    32     vs 24</p>
<p> Commerzbank (Nederland) N.V.	    16     vs 16</p>
<p> Commerzbank (South East Asia) Ltd.    33     vs 32</p>
<p> Commerzbank (Switzerland) Ltd	   39     vs 31</p>
<p> Jupiter International Group PLC	 79     vs N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - *comdirect GmbH is Commerzbank AG's direct banking subsidiary.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
